  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1035 PM CDT Wed Jun 3 2026\n\nThe ridge over the SE US will remain in a flattened state into the \nnext work week, with 700 and 850mb charts confirming a more moist, \nwarm pattern remaining in the area. As the ridge remains on the \nflatter side, shortwaves will be able to traverse Middle Tennessee \nbeginning on Sunday with our next chance for rain. Various \nshortwaves will continue to impact the region through mid-week. \nWhile we are not expecting organized severe weather at this time, \nstorms will be typical summertime storms: bubbling up in the hottest \nparts of the day, could be a strong storm or two with some gusty \nwinds or small hail, and then dissipating around sunset. As for \ntemperatures, best chance of exceeding 90 degrees looks to be late \nweekend/early next week in areas around Nashville and along the \nTennessee river. Other areas are cooler...for now. As we all know \nsummer time heat comes for us all in due time.",
